      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bearsville was named after Christian Baehr, a German peddler who opened a store on Sawkill Creek in 1839.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bearsville%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Albert Grossman turned a 15‑acre Catskill plot into a music sanctuary that hosted Bob Dylan, Janis Joplin, and The Band.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bearsvillecenter.com/pages/bearsville-history",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bearsville Center’s park offers a nature trail and hosts outdoor concerts, festivals, and community gatherings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bearsvillecenter.com/pages/bearsville-history",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Bearsville Theater, still operating after Grossman’s 1986 death, preserves the town’s artistic heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
